Luma for Raspberry Pi 5 (@VERSION@, updates from @REF@)

This card is a complete Luma system. Partition 1 (LUMA_PI5, this one) holds
config.txt, U-Boot, the device trees and GRUB; partition 2 is /boot; partition
3 is the system, which grows to fill the card on the first boot.

The first boot runs Luma's setup (language, network, your account) and takes a
few minutes while apps are imported. Update from Settings; the system updates
itself, and this partition is not rewritten by an update.

Choose the menu entry for the next boot only, from a running Luma:
  sudo luma-rpi5-boot-next uboot       (U-Boot's next boot device)
The GRUB menu on HDMI cannot be driven with a USB keyboard.
